    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Brady Singer. His combination of a 13% dynamic platoon boost and the volume associated with the #1 spot makes him an elite start. **Bryce Harper** (71.32) remains a high-floor anchor in the UTIL spot despite the platoon disadvantage against Carson Palmquist, buoyed by his elite .387 xwOBA, while **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) round out our top-tier targets. **Geraldo Perdomo** in particular sees a significant +19% boost from the matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez, making him a high-efficiency engine for our daily counting stats. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose 46.99 score narrowly missed the cut. While the optimizer appreciated the slight boost provided by his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries\u2014a key metric for our pursuit of scarce stolen bases\u2014his projected efficiency ultimately lagged behind the high-upside profiles of **Gavin Sheets** and **JJ Bleday**. Risk management remains critical today as many of our core hitters, including **Yainer Diaz**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Jonathan Aranda**, are still subject to pending lineup confirmations. We have baked in historical assumptions, but users should monitor the status of **Jonathan Aranda** closely; his +14% park factor and +12% platoon edge make him an essential piece of our lineup if he cracks the #2 spot as projected. Any late-breaking news regarding his availability or weather shifts at his venue could necessitate a quick pivot to **Gleyber Torres** or **Braden Montgomery** on the bench.",
